    </figure>
    <p>Planned for this file: the TRA outcome, the PTE score report and later the lodgement confirmation. Not as decoration, but as proof that every number in this article has a real piece of paper behind it.</p>
  </AufklappBox>

  <!-- Migration Agent -->
  <h2 id="migration-agent">The Migration Agent: why we got advice</h2>

  <p>
    So far we've had one first consultation with Johannes Kunz, a German-speaking Migration Agent. Cost: around 250 AUD (roughly 200 €). The conversation ran long, he took his time, explained everything and answered uncomfortable questions directly. What helped us most: he didn't sell us, he stress-tested us. Which risks at which route, which stream variant for our case, where the typical pitfalls sit.
  </p>

  <p>
    After the consultation we could keep asking questions by email. So far we've had an answer every time without additional cost. That convinced us. We'd recommend Johannes Kunz any day.
  </p>

  <p>
    His next job starts now: once the nomination is through, he lodges the 186 application with us so no mistakes creep in. He invoices by time spent, not flat fee. As soon as we have the concrete number, we'll add it here.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    <strong>Our experience:</strong> A Migration Agent is not mandatory, but for a 186 application with a family we wouldn't try it without one a second time. The cost of mistakes, say wrong stream choice or incomplete paperwork, is higher than the fee.
  </blockquote>

  <!-- Costs -->
  <h2 id="costs">Costs: what is paid and what is still to come</h2>

  <p>
    The short answer: paid so far are around 4,120 AUD for the Skill Assessment, 270 € for the PTE and 250 AUD for the Migration Agent. The big item is still ahead: 12,280 AUD in application fees for the four of us, due at lodgement. The numbers one by one:
  </p>

  <BentoSektion lang="en">
    <BentoKachel groesse="m" zahl="4,120 AUD" label="TRA Skill Assessment as a chef, paid" raster />
    <BentoKachel groesse="s" zahl="270 €" label="PTE Academic in Hamburg, paid" raster />
    <BentoKachel groesse="s" zahl="250 AUD" label="first consultation Migration Agent, paid" raster />
    <BentoKachel groesse="m" zahl="12,280 AUD" label="application fees for the four of us, still to come" akzent raster />
  </BentoSektion>

  <p>
    The application fees in detail: since 1 July 2026 the 186 costs 6,140 AUD for the main applicant, 3,070 AUD for an adult secondary applicant and 1,535 AUD per child under 18, per the official pricing tool of the Department of Home Affairs (<a href="https://immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/visa-pricing-estimator" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visa Pricing Estimator</a>, queried August 2026). For two adults and two children that makes 12,280 AUD. When we first wrote this article in April, the same calculation came to roughly 9,825 AUD. Between planning and lodging, fees can rise, in our case by around 2,500 AUD.
  </p>

  <AufklappBox titel="Open the full cost table" lang="en">
    <div class="tabellen-halter">
      <table class="kosten-tabelle">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>What</th>
